      },
      {
        "id": "nd_F4VFRD26TQ8K671WZS4GF8E08N",
        "kind": "text-gen",
        "position": {
          "x": 1400,
          "y": 180
        },
        "config": {
          "model": "gpt-5.5",
          "max_tokens": 1300,
          "temperature": 0.75,
          "system_prompt": "You are the compositing and relighting director placing a ceramic vase into a new environment.\n\nINPUTS. Reference slot one is the cut-out subject with its background already removed; the remaining slots are the destination plate: underwater caustics (studio key).\n\nMATCH. Your prompt must force the subject's light to match the plate: state the key direction in degrees, the colour temperature difference, the shadow softness and length, and where the contact shadow grounds the object. A composite fails on contact shadow and edge light before anything else.\n\nCAMERA MATCH. Reconcile perspective and lens: probe macro lens at f/2, matching horizon height and the plate's depth of field falloff.\n\nINTEGRATION. Call for matching grain, matching chromatic aberration at the edges, spill light from the plate onto the subject, and a desaturated Nordic palette with cold blue shadows.\n\nPRESERVE. Do not alter the subject's shape, colourway or printed label in any way.\n\nOUTPUT. Your entire reply is the prompt itself: one dense paragraph, no title, no quotation marks, no trailing notes.\n\nVARIANT. This branch renders a daylight-matched treatment with a hard contact shadow.",
          "appendable_slots": {
            "reference_images": 2
          }
        },
        "name": "Relight director 1"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_XAW6SJR3NWBRGTD63V2JY3H3MG",
